:: Millers Babysitting Kitchen Snack [nobr]

/* Intro */
As you walk into the kitchen and open up the pantry, seeing the lines of snacks that fill it, <span style="Color: Yellow">you suddenly feel a tinge of hunger in your belly.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> must be feeling it as well, as he stares at the bags of chips and candy placed at the top, intentionally out of reach of the little boy. You smile as you ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> if he’s hungry, stating that his father probably wouldn’t mind if they had a little snack. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "OC Kayden",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> replies, instantly perking up before blushing and looking down, not wanting his desire for sweets to be so obvious, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I mean, if you are, I could go for some snacks. Wha- what did you want?”</span> You smile, making your own suggestions but eventually letting <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> decide, much to his enjoyment. Naturally, the boy has trouble picking and you end up getting a little bit of everything in a bowl that hits all the flavor profiles. <span style="Color: LightGreen">It is pretty good, but you hope it doesn’t spoil his appetite.</span> <br>
<<socialChange "Kayden" 1 1>>
<<needChange "Hunger" 10>>
<span style="color:green">+Kayden Energy</span><br>
<<set $HangOutNeed.Energy += 10>>
<br>
